<section class="section section--flush hero"><img src="/assets/img/projects/control-room-combined-cycle-hero.jpg" alt="Combined-cycle plant control room with operator consoles and overview display" width="2400" height="800" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><div class="container prose"><h1>Control systems written by process engineers</h1><p>We design, commission and maintain control systems for power plants and refineries. The difference between us and an automation contractor shows up in the fuel bill.</p><p class="hero-actions"><a href="/references.html" class="btn btn--primary">References</a><a href="/combined-cycle-power-plants.html" class="btn btn--secondary">Combined Cycle Power Plants</a></p></div></section><section class="section section--tint"><div class="container prose"><h2 class="section-title">What we do that others do not</h2><p>Six DCS platforms and experience on SIL 2 and SIL 3 applications are the baseline. What sets us apart is the process engineering behind the control system.</p><h3>Island mode, proven on a running plant</h3><p>When a refinery loses the grid, its CHP plant has seconds to decide whether the refinery keeps running. We implemented that transition and proved it on a live plant in two trials, holding 13–14 MW in the island, agreed in advance with the transmission and distribution system operators. It is one of the most demanding tests in power plant commissioning and most contractors are never asked to run it.</p><p><a href="/island-mode/">Island mode operation</a></p>
<h3>Fuel accounting inside the control system</h3><p>A CHP plant makes two products from one fuel stream, and no measurement separates them. We implement the allocation, the boiler efficiency by direct and indirect method, and the turbine heat balance as live calculations in the DCS, archived, with the cost of every deviation from design attached. Most plants get this as a spreadsheet at month end, if at all.</p><p><a href="/plant-performance.html">Plant performance and fuel accounting</a></p>
<h3>Combustion that follows the fuel</h3><p>On a CFB boiler firing petroleum coke, the fuel changes constantly. We calculate its calorific value automatically from the combustion result and distribute solid fuel across the feeders by heat value. That control strategy cannot be written without understanding what is happening in the furnace.</p><p><a href="/projects/advanced-controllers-cfb-boiler.html">Advanced controllers for CFB boilers</a></p>
<h3>Eleven years on one plant — and back again</h3><p>Three boilers of 120 t/h, a 260 t/h CFB boiler, three 12 MW turbines and one of 30 MW, five steam headers, a refinery on the other end. Designed, commissioned and maintained continuously from 2007 to 2018, and under maintenance again since 2022. Process knowledge of a plant is not bought; it accumulates.</p><p><a href="/references.html">References</a></p></div></section><section class="section"><div class="container prose"><h2 class="section-title">What we do</h2><ul class="link-index"><li><a href="/service/process-automation.html">Process Automation</a><span class="link-index__line">DCS and ESD from design through commissioning.</span></li>
<li><a href="/service/process-optimization-advanced-process-control.html">Process optimisation / Advanced process control</a><span class="link-index__line">DCS optimisers for load, fuel and emissions, delivered as a set.</span></li>
<li><a href="/service/manufacturing-execution-system.html">MES (Manufacturing Execution System)</a><span class="link-index__line">Production data, efficiency and loss analysis over OPC.</span></li>
<li><a href="/service/safety-systems-burner-management-systems.html">Safety Systems and Burner Management Systems</a><span class="link-index__line">BMS and SIS to SIL 2 and SIL 3 under IEC 61511.</span></li>
<li><a href="/service/industrial-furniture-control-centers.html">Industrial furniture / Control centers</a><span class="link-index__line">ISO 11064 control room design and operator furniture.</span></li>
<li><a href="/service/maintenance.html">Maintenance</a><span class="link-index__line">Lifecycle support for major DCS platforms.</span></li></ul></div></section><section class="section section--tint"><div class="container prose"><h2 class="section-title">Industries</h2><ul class="link-index"><li><a href="/industries/power-generation.html">Power Generation</a><span class="link-index__line">Automation for steam, gas and hydro turbines, HRSG, boilers and district heating.</span></li>
<li><a href="/industries/oil-and-gas.html">Oil and Gas</a><span class="link-index__line">Burner management, safety instrumented systems and control room architecture.</span></li>
<li><a href="/industries/cement-and-coal.html">Bulk material handling</a><span class="link-index__line">Conveyors, bins, crushers, mills and weigh batching — from concrete plants to solid fuel handling on boilers.</span></li>
<li><a href="/industries/control-centers.html">Control Centers</a><span class="link-index__line">Design, manufacture and supply of control centers and operator furniture.</span></li></ul></div></section><section class="section"><div class="container prose"><h2 class="section-title">Selected projects</h2><h3><a href="/projects/advanced-controllers-cfb-boiler.html">Advanced Controllers for CFB Boilers</a></h3><div class="section-promo__layout section-promo__layout--card"><figure class="figure--embed"><a href="/projects/advanced-controllers-cfb-boiler.html"><img src="/assets/img/2024/08/10/advanced_boiler_load_controllers.jpg" alt="Advanced load controllers for CFB boiler" width="635" height="505" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></a><figcaption>Advanced load controllers for CFB boiler</figcaption></figure><div class="section-promo__text"><p>260 t/h at 100 bar, firing petroleum coke, coal, gas and fuel oil, with the coke calorific value calculated automatically from the combustion result.</p><p><a href="/projects/advanced-controllers-cfb-boiler.html">Read more</a></p></div></div>
<h3><a href="/projects/power-plant-performance-calculation.html">Power Plant Performance Calculation</a></h3><div class="section-promo__layout section-promo__layout--card"><figure class="figure--embed"><a href="/projects/power-plant-performance-calculation.html"><img src="/assets/img/projects/steam-turbine-generator-hall.jpg" alt="Hydro turbine and generator set in the machine hall" width="960" height="640" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></a><figcaption>Hydro turbine and generator set in the machine hall</figcaption></figure><div class="section-promo__text"><p>Boiler, turbine and heat exchanger efficiency against design values, live in the control system, with the cost of each deviation attached.</p><p><a href="/projects/power-plant-performance-calculation.html">Read more</a></p></div></div>
<h3><a href="/projects/virtual-power-plant.html">Virtual Power Plant</a></h3><div class="section-promo__layout section-promo__layout--card"><figure class="figure--embed"><a href="/projects/virtual-power-plant.html"><img src="/assets/img/2024/08/10/virtual-power-plant-vpp.jpg" alt="Virtual power plant combining renewable and conventional generation" width="635" height="505" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></a><figcaption>Virtual power plant combining renewable and conventional generation</figcaption></figure><div class="section-promo__text"><p>A CHP plant, four photovoltaic plants and an 80 MW wind farm dispatched as one balancing group, with the steam turbine as the regulating machine.</p><p><a href="/projects/virtual-power-plant.html">Read more</a></p></div></div></div></section><section class="section section--tint"><div class="container prose"><p>See the full project list under <a href="/references.html">References</a>. SIL 2 and SIL 3 on HIMA HIQuad, Foxboro Triconex and ABB AC800; DCS on Emerson Ovation; remote dispatch over IEC 60870-5-104. We also manufacture our own DIN-rail automation modules, taken through the applicable EU conformity assessment procedures — see <a href="/homemaster/">HomeMaster</a> and <a href="/compliance.html">Compliance and Testing</a>.</p></div></section>
